Original commit body from eda96149e027e759fbf88644d6433323b48b8728:

runtime-cli-no-network said embeddings downloads happen only through the
install path. It was false: install-embeddings, add-extras and
`pip install 'hypergumbo[embeddings]'` installed only the library, and
_load_st_model_offline_first fell back to a network-allowed
SentenceTransformer(name) on a cache miss, so the first sketch fetched
microsoft/unixcoder-base and nomic-ai/modernbert-embed-base from
huggingface.co. Measured in the 2026-10-25 premise check with a stub
sentence_transformers: every cache miss was a local_files_only=True
attempt followed by a download-allowed retry. The degradation warning
also told users install-embeddings would cache the weights, which it did
not.

The claim is kept and the code made to match it (the owner's 2026-08-11
ruling on the same choice for repo_inspection: declare, don't launder):

- The runtime loader is cache-only: a miss raises EmbeddingsUnavailable
  naming `hypergumbo install-embeddings`, after restoring the caller's
  HF_HUB_OFFLINE; and _ensure_hf_offline_for_cached_models now forces
  offline on every runtime load, closing the partial-cache window it left
  open only so the runtime download could proceed.
- sketch_embeddings.fetch_embedding_models is the one place a model is
  fetched; install-embeddings (including the already-installed path) and
  add-extras run it in a fresh interpreter and fail when it fails.
- The warning, runtime-cli-no-network, the spec, both READMEs and
  SECURITY.md say what happens now; the README's open-findings list also
  drops INV-tusos and INV-kuroj, fixed in #1856 and #1857.
- I/O allowlist: the two loader sites lose the finding (cache-only), the
  fetch and its subprocess are listed under the install zone.

Tests: test_embeddings_never_fetched_at_runtime.py (14; it could not import
before the change). Seven existing tests pinned the runtime download as
intended behaviour -- the fallback, its kwargs, its ValueError arm, its
offline restore, the "first-install download is still reached" control
and two partial-cache "leave offline off" checks -- and are inverted, each
saying so. Three install tests now pin the model-cache state, which they
had silently depended on. check-self-claims: 18 claims unchanged (18
confirmed_with_caveats).

Behaviour change: a sketch after `pip install 'hypergumbo[embeddings]'`
without install-embeddings now runs without embeddings and says to run it.

Addresses INV-gujus.

